Short:        Open RTG system with OpenGPU and Warp3D
Uploader:     (We fill this in at upload time)
Author:       Dalsin Limited
Type:         driver/video
Version:      0.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

OpenRTG is a free RTG (retargetable graphics) system for AmigaOS 3.x:
openrtg.library opens screens on graphics cards and draws on them, beside an
installed Picasso96, with one of the two active at a time.

Planned, as the design in DESIGN.md sets out:
- several monitors as standard (two RTG monitors and AGA), up to four;
- OpenGPU, one acceleration layer for 2D, compositing, 3D and batched maths,
  with a driver for each chip and the CPU as fallback;
- Warp3D built in, through one hardware driver for every chip OpenGPU drives;
- an OS 4 look for windows on Workbench, as OS-friendly resident patches;
- one GadTools prefs editor for monitors, screen modes, colours and the look;
- OS 4's RTG calls by name, so code moves between OS 3 and OS 4;
- Picasso96 card drivers work under it, so real cards (Picasso IV, CyberVision
  64, ZZ9000) and a PiStorm's RTG keep working.

Status: this archive is the design and LibCount, the measuring tool of phase 0
(also on Aminet as dev/debug/libcount). openrtg.library is in development;
AmigaChrome (an Amiga for the PC) runs the first several-monitor setup today.

